    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **255 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date on `POST /api/owners`, responding with 400, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectFutureRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a reject step (`@Val Owner`) that throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException` when the supplied `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`; a null/omitted date passes through.\n- `FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler mapping it to 400 Bad Request via `ProblemDetail`, matching the existing `InvalidPostcode` handler pattern.\n- `...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` between `build` and `defaultRegistrationDate`.\n\n**Key design decision:** the reject step runs *before* `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`, so it inspects the date exactly as supplied \u2014 before defaulting (null \u2192 today) or the weekend/holiday business-day roll-forward could otherwise mask or alter the check.",
